{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JgdKuobyoXVEUJNeh4dV3F","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tFrom: Deniz Arı <deniz.ari@freya.example>\n2\tTo: Selin Aydın <selin.aydin@freyabank.example>\n3\tCc: Kerem Yalçın <kerem.yalcin@freyabank.example>, Burcu Tan <burcu.tan@freyabank.example>, Elçin Ural <elcin.ural@freyabank.example>, Ozan Er <ozan.er@freya.example>\n4\tDate: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 17:48:12 +0300\n5\tSubject: Re: Statement debt - what we took away from Wednesday\n6\t\n7\tThanks Selin, clear. Three calming replies it is, I've fixed it on our side.\n8\t\n9\tOn the card number: noted. Our mocks follow the test environment for now,\n10\tbut we'll build the last-six and full-number steps as agreed, so they work\n11\tonce the service sends full numbers.\n12\t\n13\tDeniz\n14\t\n15\t-----\n16\t\n17\tOn 9 Oct 2026, at 15:02, Selin Aydın <selin.aydin@freyabank.example> wrote:\n18\t\n19\t> Hi Deniz,\n20\t>\n21\t> Thanks for writing this up, saves me a job. Yes, the points below apply,\n22\t> with one correction further down. I haven't had time to put them into the\n23\t> analysis document yet, so the one I sent yesterday (8 Oct) won't show them,\n24\t> especially the out-of-scope part and the card number. Please build to these.\n25\t>\n26\t> One correction: on the angry caller it was three calming replies, not two.\n27\t> Burcu wanted room for the caller to settle before we hand over. Only if they\n28\t> are still complaining after the third one do we say \"Sizi müşteri\n29\t> temsilcimize aktarıyorum.\" and transfer to an agent. And the assistant never\n30\t> answers insults in kind, whatever the count.\n31\t>\n32\t> Also, Elçin raised this after you'd dropped off: the card list service in\n33\t> production gives the full card number. What you see in the test environment\n34\t> is masked (first six and last four), that's a test-data thing only, so please\n35\t> don't design around it. Whatever comes back, the assistant never reads out\n36\t> more than the last four digits of a card, not the full number and not the\n37\t> middle digits, not even to confirm.\n38\t>\n39\t> Kerem, anything to add on the card list?\n40\t>\n41\t> Selin\n42\t>\n43\t> On 9 Oct 2026, at 10:14, Deniz Arı <deniz.ari@freya.example> wrote:\n44\t>\n45\t>> Hi Selin,\n46\t>>\n47\t>> Thanks again for Wednesday, long session but very useful. Below is what I\n48\t>> noted down as agreed on the statement debt flow. It's not everything we\n49\t>> talked about, just the points that change what we're building. Shout if I\n50\t>> got anything wrong.\n51\t>>\n52\t>> 1. Silence. If the caller says nothing, the assistant asks the question\n53\t>>    again, shortly, the first two times. On the third silence it says\n54\t>>    \"Sesinizi alamadığım için görüşmeyi sonlandırıyorum.\" and ends the call.\n55\t>>    No main menu in this case.\n56\t>>\n57\t>> 2. Questions outside the flow (e.g. loan rates, branch hours). The assistant\n58\t>>    doesn't send the caller away straight off; it first asks\n59\t>>    \"Size bu konuda yardımcı olamıyorum. Sizi ana menüye aktarmamı ister misiniz?\"\n60\t>>    Yes -> main menu. If they'd rather go on, we pick the flow back up where\n61\t>>    it was. If the answer isn't clear, ask again, three tries.\n62\t>>\n63\t>> 3. Three tries used up at any question: \"Size şu anda yardımcı olamıyorum.\n64\t>>    Sizi ana menüye aktarıyorum.\" then main menu. Asking us to repeat\n65\t>>    something we just read doesn't count as a try.\n66\t>>\n67\t>> 4. Two cards with the same name and the same last four digits: we ask for\n68\t>>    the last six, \"Son dört hanesi 4253 olan birden fazla kartınız var.\n69\t>>    Kartınızın son altı hanesini söyler misiniz?\" (with the caller's own\n70\t>>    digits), and if those match too, the full number: \"Son altı hanesi aynı\n71\t>>    olan birden fazla kartınız var. Kart numaranızı söyler misiniz?\"\n72\t>>\n73\t>> 5. Angry or abusive caller: up to two calming replies, then agent.\n74\t>>\n75\t>> 6. Currencies are always read with their full names, never the codes:\n76\t>>    Türk Lirası, Dolar, Euro, İngiliz Sterlini. Also where the table in the\n77\t>>    document says \"TL\".\n78\t>>\n79\t>> I've left out the statement week and the joint statement points, Ozan is\n80\t>> writing those up separately with the sample sentences. Still open on our\n81\t>> side: how long we wait on a slow service before handing over, we'll come\n82\t>> back with a proposal.\n83\t>>\n84\t>> Best,\n85\t>> Deniz"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01S2HeanQ121N3iUrzXcmepZ","session_id":"adf52405-6942-4d44-9d85-c3233da23ca1","uuid":"a851a948-a9de-4a7e-a9b4-1360770fd075","timestamp":"2026-10-11T19:19:18.386Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write rules.md from docs"}
