{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UauxeYzoYuDW3DXsQaMKfn","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tHome > Personal > Cards > Help centre > Credit cards: statements and payments\n2\t\n3\t[Skip to content]   Log in   |   Become a customer   |   Branches & ATMs\n4\t\n5\tWe use cookies to make this site work better. Accept all  /  Manage settings\n6\t\n7\t# Credit cards: statements and payments\n8\t\n9\tAnswers to the questions we hear most often about your Yıldız credit card statement and how to pay it. Can't find what you need? Scroll to the bottom for ways to reach us.\n10\t\n11\t---\n12\t\n13\t**When will I get my statement?**\n14\t\n15\tOnce a month, on your statement date. Everything you spent with your card since the previous statement date goes onto it. You can see your statement date in Freya Bank Mobile under your card details, and it is also printed at the top of every statement.\n16\t\n17\t**Can I change my statement date?**\n18\t\n19\tYes. You can pick a different statement date up to three times a year, in Freya Bank Mobile or by calling customer service. The new date applies from your next statement onwards. Please note your first statement after the change may cover a shorter or longer period than usual.\n20\t\n21\t**How do I get my statement by e-mail?**\n22\t\n23\tJust tell us where you'd like it sent. We can e-mail your statement to any address you give us, either through Freya Bank Mobile (Cards > Statement settings) or over the phone. E-mailed statements come as a PDF.\n24\t\n25\t**I didn't receive my statement. What should I do?**\n26\t\n27\tFirst check your spam or junk folder. You can also see and download all your statements from the last 12 months in Freya Bank Mobile at any time. If it's still missing, contact customer service and we'll send it again.\n28\t\n29\t**What is the minimum payment?**\n30\t\n31\tIt is the smallest amount you need to pay by the due date to keep your card in good standing. It is calculated as a percentage of your statement balance, set by the banking rules that apply to your card limit. The exact amount is shown on your statement and in the app.\n32\t\n33\t**What happens if I only pay the minimum?**\n34\t\n35\tYour card stays in good standing, but interest is charged on the part of the balance you didn't pay. Paying the full statement balance is the only way to avoid interest.\n36\t\n37\t**And if I pay less than the minimum, or nothing?**\n38\t\n39\tLate payment interest is charged and it may affect your credit record. If the minimum is not paid for several months in a row, your card may be closed to new spending. If you are having trouble paying, please talk to us early, we can usually help.\n40\t\n41\t**When is my payment due?**\n42\t\n43\tYour due date is shown on your statement, usually about 10 days after the statement date. If the due date falls on a weekend or public holiday, it moves to the next working day.\n44\t\n45\t**I spent in dollars, euros or pounds. How is that shown?**\n46\t\n47\tSpending in a foreign currency is shown on your statement in that currency, separately from your Turkish lira spending. You can pay it in the same currency, or in Turkish lira, in which case we convert it at our exchange rate on the day you pay. Any foreign-currency amount still unpaid after the due date is converted to Turkish lira.\n48\t\n49\t**How can I pay my card?**\n50\t\n51\t- In Freya Bank Mobile: Cards > select your card > Pay. You can pay from any of your Freya Bank accounts.\n52\t- At any Freya Bank branch, in cash or from your account.\n53\t- At Freya Bank ATMs, with or without a card.\n54\t- Automatically: set up automatic payment and we'll take the minimum or the full amount from your account on the due date.\n55\t\n56\tPayments in the app or at an ATM show on your card straight away. (Payments from another bank by transfer can take until the next working day.)\n57\t\n58\t**Can I pay my card over the phone?**\n59\t\n60\tYou can check your balance and statement details on the phone line. For payments we recommend Freya Bank Mobile, it's the quickest way.\n61\t\n62\t**Can I split my statement into instalments?**\n63\t\n64\tFor some purchases, yes, depending on the merchant and your card. Eligible transactions show an \"Instalment\" option in Freya Bank Mobile. Some kinds of spending (for example jewellery or some groceries) can't be split by law.\n65\t\n66\t**There's a transaction on my statement I don't recognise. What do I do?**\n67\t\n68\tPlease contact customer service as soon as possible, by phone or through the \"Messages\" section in Freya Bank Mobile. Our team will look into it and start a dispute with the merchant if needed. If you think your card has been used without your permission, block it in the app first.\n69\t\n70\t**Is my statement the same for all my cards?**\n71\t\n72\tIf you have more than one Yıldız card, each card gets its own statement, unless you have asked for a joint statement. Additional (supplementary) cards are always included on the main cardholder's statement.\n73\t\n74\t---\n75\t\n76\tWas this page helpful?   Yes  /  No\n77\t\n78\tStill need help? Call our customer service line, available 24/7, or visit your nearest branch.\n79\t\n80\tRelated: Card limits | Lost or stolen card | Fees and charges | Yıldız card benefits\n81\t\n82\tPublished 14 August 2025"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01S2HeanQ121N3iUrzXcmepZ","session_id":"adf52405-6942-4d44-9d85-c3233da23ca1","uuid":"6b8c6525-8d4f-4a90-a54c-abde17f27daf","timestamp":"2026-10-11T19:19:30.212Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write rules.md from docs"}
