{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YAa1z1koV3WhiZQGkyYKF3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Statement debt: self-service step for the voice assistant\n2\t\n3\tBusiness analysis, working draft\n4\tAuthor: Selin Aydın (Card Self-Service, Freya Bank)\n5\tDate: 2 September 2026\n6\tShared with: Kerem Yalçın, Burcu Tan, Mert Koç (for the service part)\n7\t\n8\t> Kerem, Burcu: this is my first pass after the two walkthroughs of the phone menu. Comments inline please, I'll collect them before we sit down with the Freya team. Anything marked **TBD** I could not close myself.\n9\t\n10\t---\n11\t\n12\t## 0. In one paragraph\n13\t\n14\tToday the menu plays a fixed announcement and that's it. With the assistant we want a short conversation instead: which card, how much is owed and by when, and then two things the caller can get done without waiting for an agent (statement PDF by mail, a different statement week). Paying stays with the agents for now. Whatever else the caller brings up, we hand back to the main menu.\n15\t\n16\t## 1. Scope\n17\t\n18\tIn:\n19\t- Debt reading for one card at a time, all four currencies we carry (Lira, Dollar, Euro, Sterling), with the due date. When the closed statement is fully paid, the \"no debt\" wording plus the running total.\n20\t- The two follow-ups: mailing the statement (only ever to the address we hold) and moving the statement week.\n21\t- Choosing the card, where needed.\n22\t\n23\tOut (first list, Kerem please extend):\n24\t- Paying the debt itself: handed to an agent.\n25\t- Disputes, \"I paid but it doesn't show\" (agent, see §7).\n26\t- Limits, cash advance, card blocking, anything about debit cards.\n27\t- Changing the e-mail address.\n28\t- Statements of earlier periods.\n29\t\n30\tBurcu thinks statement debt is one of the top three menu choices; she'll try to get a figure.\n31\t\n32\t## 2. How the caller arrives\n33\t\n34\tThe phone menu has already identified and authenticated the caller before the hand-over. The assistant receives the customer number with the call and does not run any identity check of its own.\n35\t\n36\t**TBD:** the flow drawing we got from the vendor side has a box \"second factor may be needed\". I don't see why for a read-only step plus two low-risk actions; to confirm with Elçin.\n37\t\n38\t## 3. Picking the card\n39\t\n40\tThe card list comes from `cards.list` (customer number in, eligible credit cards out). Then:\n41\t\n42\t| Situation | What the assistant does |\n43\t|---|---|\n44\t| Caller already named the card when arriving | If the name fits exactly one card, no selection question. |\n45\t| Several cards | Asks which one, with at most two example names taken from the caller's own cards: “Hangi kartınızın borcunu öğrenmek istersiniz? Örneğin, Yıldız Premium veya Yıldız Pratik diyebilirsiniz.” |\n46\t| Caller asks for \"all my cards\" | Not possible, the debt service takes one card at a time. Selection question again (counts as a failed attempt). |\n47\t| Name not on the list | Tells the caller there is no card with that name and reads the eligible ones again. |\n48\t| Two or more cards with the same name | Asks for the last four digits: “Yıldız isimli birden fazla kartınız var. Kartınızın son dört hanesini söyler misiniz?” (name of the card in place of \"Yıldız\") |\n49\t| Same name and same last four | Asks for the full card number: “Son dört hanesi aynı olan birden fazla kartınız var. Kart numaranızın tamamını söyler misiniz?” |\n50\t\n51\tTwo easy cases outside the table: a single card is simply taken, no question. No eligible card at all: “Ekstre borcunu sorgulayabileceğiniz uygun bir kredi kartınız bulunmuyor. Sizi ana menüye yönlendiriyorum.”\n52\t\n53\tNotes:\n54\t- Digits can come as \"dört iki beş üç\", \"kırk iki elli üç\" etc. The assistant maps them to the four digits and moves on. No reading back of the digits, no \"… kartınızla devam ediyorum\" confirmation; the card name is said anyway at the start of the debt reading.\n55\t- Supplementary card holders: they see no eligible card of their own here. Tell them and ask for a different card. (Burcu, is that what the menu does today?)\n56\t- If the card name comes back empty from the service, introduce the card by its last four only.\n57\t\n58\t## 4. Reading the debt\n59\t\n60\tService: `cards.balance` with the chosen card. It returns one block per currency (`debtTL`, `debtUSD`, `debtEUR`, `debtGBP`) with `statementDebt`, `minPayment`, `remainingDebt`, `remainingMinPayment`, `totalDebt`, plus `statementDate`, `lastPayDate`.\n61\t\n62\tOrder:\n63\t1. Card introduction + statement date (glued to the first currency).\n64\t2. Turkish Lira.\n65\t3. Dollar, then Euro, then Sterling (only the ones with debt).\n66\t4. One sentence for the currencies with no debt.\n67\t5. Remaining auto-payment amount, when there is one (**TBD**, see §9).\n68\t6. Due date.\n69\t7. If the caller has more eligible cards: “Başka bir kartınızın borcunu öğrenmek ister misiniz?”\n70\t8. Offer (§5).\n71\t\n72\tCard introduction, example on the Lira line:\n73\t“Sonu dört iki beş üç ile biten Yıldız Premium kartınıza ait 21 Ağustos 2026 tarihinde kesilen ekstre Türk Lirası borcunuz …”\n74\t\n75\t### Turkish Lira: three cases by what has been paid\n76\t\n77\t| Paid so far | Sentence |\n78\t|---|---|\n79\t| Nothing | “Türk Lirası borcunuz XXX TL, ödenmesi gereken minimum tutar ZZZ TL'dir.” |\n80\t| Minimum or more | “Türk Lirası borcunuz XXX TL, kalan toplam borcunuz YYY TL'dir. Minimum ödemenizi yaptığınız için teşekkür ederiz.” |\n81\t| Less than the minimum | “Türk Lirası borcunuz XXX TL, ödenmesi gereken minimum tutar ZZZ TL, kalan toplam borcunuz YYY TL, kalan minimum ödeme tutarınız TTT TL'dir.” |\n82\t\n83\tXXX statementDebt, ZZZ minPayment, YYY remainingDebt, TTT remainingMinPayment.\n84\tHow I pick the case (Mert to check): debt only if remainingDebt > 0; \"nothing paid\" if remainingMinPayment equals or exceeds minPayment; \"minimum or more\" if remainingMinPayment is zero or below; \"less than minimum\" otherwise. If remainingDebt is 0,00 we go to the no-debt wording for Lira.\n85\t\n86\tNo Lira debt → Lira is skipped and goes into the no-debt sentence.\n87\t\n88\t### Foreign currencies\n89\t\n90\tSame pattern for all three, no paid/unpaid split:\n91\t\n92\t“Dolar borcunuz XXX USD, kalan toplam borcunuz YYY USD, ödenmesi gereken minimum tutar ZZZ USD'dir.”\n93\tEuro and Sterling the same way (EUR, GBP; \"İngiliz Sterlini borcunuz …\").\n94\t\n95\t### Currencies without debt\n96\t\n97\tOne sentence at the end. My table (not all 15 lines yet, I'll fill the rest):\n98\t\n99\t| TL | USD | EUR | GBP | Sentence |\n100\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n101\t| debt | – | – | debt | “Dolar ve Euro borcunuz bulunmamaktadır.” |\n102\t| debt | debt | – | – | “Euro ve İngiliz Sterlini borcunuz bulunmamaktadır.” |\n103\t| debt | – | debt | – | “Dolar ve İngiliz Sterlini borcunuz bulunmamaktadır.” |\n104\t| – | debt | debt | debt | “TL borcunuz bulunmamaktadır.” |\n105\t| – | debt | – | – | “TL, Euro ve İngiliz Sterlini borcunuz bulunmamaktadır.” |\n106\t| – | – | debt | – | “TL, Dolar ve İngiliz Sterlini borcunuz bulunmamaktadır.” |\n107\t| debt | debt | debt | debt | nothing, all four are read |\n108\t| … | | | | TBD |\n109\t\n110\tNegative amounts (credit balance) and zero count as \"no debt\" in that currency. A currency the card does not carry at all: **TBD** whether it goes into this sentence.\n111\t\n112\t### Due date\n113\t\n114\t“Borçlarınız için son ödeme tarihiniz 16 Eylül 2026'dır.” (date from lastPayDate)\n115\t\n116\tIf the due date is today, say \"bugün\": “Borçlarınız için son ödeme tarihiniz bugündür.”\n117\t\n118\t### No statement debt\n119\t\n120\t“Sonu [son 4 hane] ile biten [kart adı] kartınızın [hesap kesim tarihi] tarihli ekstresinden borcunuz bulunmamaktadır. Gelecek dönemler dahil toplam borcunuz GGG TL'dir. Son ödeme tarihiniz [son ödeme tarihi] olacaktır.”\n121\t\n122\tThen the other-card question if there is another eligible card. Otherwise main menu. (Kerem: do we offer e-mail/statement week here too? I lean no, nothing to send.)\n123\t\n124\t### How things are spoken\n125\t\n126\t- Amounts: lira and kuruş in full (\"bir milyon iki yüz otuz dört bin beş yüz altmış yedi lira seksen dokuz kuruş\"); zero kuruş is dropped (\"iki bin beş yüz Türk Lirası\"). Dollar/Euro decimals as cents, Sterling as pence.\n127\t- Dates: day, month name, year (\"21 Ağustos 2026\").\n128\t- Last four digits one by one: \"dört iki beş üç\", \"bir sıfır sıfır üç\". Never \"kırk iki elli üç\", never \"çift sıfır\".\n129\t- The full card number is never said.\n130\t- Every amount and date exactly as the service gave it. Nothing the service did not return is said (no guessing of rates, dates or addresses).\n131\t\n132\t## 5. The offer\n133\t\n134\tAfter the due date (and after the other-card question when it applies):\n135\t\n136\t“Hesap kesim tarihinizi değiştirebilirim ya da ekstrenizi kayıtlı mail adresinize gönderebilirim.”\n137\t\n138\tOnly what the caller can actually do is offered:\n139\t- no registered e-mail → only the statement week (\"Hesap kesim tarihinizi değiştirebilirim.\");\n140\t- statement week cannot be changed → only the e-mail;\n141\t- neither → no offer.\n142\t\n143\tThat means the contact lookup (`contact.email.get`) has to run before the offer, not after the caller picks e-mail. Mert, OK?\n144\t\n145\t**TBD:** we have no way to know in advance whether the caller may still change the week (see §6.2).\n146\t\n147\tAnswers:\n148\t\n149\t| Caller says | Goes to |\n150\t|---|---|\n151\t| e-mail | §6.1 |\n152\t| change statement date / week | §6.2 |\n153\t| no / nothing else / thanks, bye | main menu, “Sizi ana menüye yönlendiriyorum.” |\n154\t| wants to pay | agent, “Borç ödeme işleminiz için sizi müşteri temsilcimize aktarıyorum.” |\n155\t| debt + e-mail in the same sentence | read the debt, then go straight to e-mail without the offer question |\n156\t\n157\t## 6. Actions\n158\t\n159\t### 6.1 Statement by e-mail\n160\t\n161\tOnly to the address the bank holds. The assistant never takes an address from the caller.\n162\t\n163\t1. `contact.email.get` (customer number). Empty address, or only a phone registered → no suitable e-mail. If the caller asks anyway: “Bankamızda kayıtlı bir e-posta adresiniz bulunmadığı için ekstrenizi gönderemiyorum.” Then statement week if possible, else main menu.\n164\t2. Read the address back and ask: “Ekstrenizi … adresine göndermemi ister misiniz?” Readable addresses as they are; long or odd ones shortened (\"m ile başlayan Gmail adresiniz\"), no spelling letter by letter.\n165\t3. Only on a clear yes: `statement.pdf.send` with card, customer number, the registered address and the statement date.\n166\t4. “Ekstreniz kayıtlı e-posta adresinize gönderildi.” then “Sizi ana menüye yönlendiriyorum.”\n167\t\n168\tOther answers:\n169\t- No → nothing sent, main menu.\n170\t- \"That address is wrong / I don't use it anymore\" → nothing sent; it cannot be changed here; main menu.\n171\t- \"Send it to another address\" → only the registered address is possible.\n172\t- \"Send last month's\" → only the last closed statement.\n173\t- Sending again in the same call: max three, then main menu.\n174\t- Service error → “Şu anda işleminizi gerçekleştiremiyorum, sizi müşteri temsilcimize aktarıyorum.”\n175\t\n176\t### 6.2 Changing the statement week\n177\t\n178\tServices: `statement.week.get` (current), `statement.week.decide` (preview, changes nothing), `statement.week.change` (the change).\n179\t\n180\t1. Current state: “[kart adı] kartınızın hesap kesim tarihi her ayın [hafta]. haftası olarak tanımlı. Bir sonraki hesap kesim tarihiniz [tarih], son ödeme tarihiniz [tarih]. Hesap kesim tarihinizi değiştirmek ister misiniz?” No → main menu.\n181\t   Joint statement: also read the main and the linked card (names, week, next closing and due dates).\n182\t2. Options, without the current week: “Hesap kesim tarihinizi ayın 1., 3. ya da 4. haftasına alabilirim. Hangisini tercih edersiniz?”\n183\t   - A week or a date we didn't offer → only the offered weeks; read them again.\n184\t   - The current week → no change needed.\n185\t3. Preview with the chosen week and the current statement day.\n186\t4. Confirm: “Yeni hesap kesim haftanız her ayın 3. haftası olacak. Yeni hesap kesim tarihiniz [tarih], son ödeme tarihiniz [tarih] olacak. Onaylıyor musunuz?”\n187\t   Joint statement: after the question, add “Bu değişiklik kartınıza bağlı [bağlı kart adı] kartınızı da etkileyecek.”\n188\t   - Only a clear \"evet\" counts. \"Olabilir\", \"sanırım\" → ask once more, clearly (three tries).\n189\t   - No → no change, “Sizi ana menüye yönlendiriyorum.”\n190\t5. `statement.week.change`, only after preview + clear yes.\n191\t6. “Sonu [son 4 hane] ile biten [kart adı] kartınızın hesap kesim haftası her ayın 3. haftası olarak değiştirildi. Yeni hesap kesim tarihiniz [tarih], son ödeme tarihiniz [tarih].” Dates from the preview (the change call does not return them). Then main menu.\n192\t\n193\tAny of the three services fails → “Şu anda hesap kesim tarihinizi değiştiremiyorum, sizi müşteri temsilcimize aktarıyorum.”\n194\t\n195\tHow often a caller may change: **TBD**. Burcu says the menu has its own limits today; I need the exact rule and whether any service tells us beforehand.\n196\t\n197\t## 7. Exits and general behaviour\n198\t\n199\t| When | Where | Sentence |\n200\t|---|---|---|\n201\t| Done / nothing else / goodbye after the reading | Main menu | “Sizi ana menüye yönlendiriyorum.” |\n202\t| Caller asks for something else mid-flow | Main menu, the request is passed on | “Sizi ana menüye yönlendiriyorum.” |\n203\t| Out-of-scope question | Main menu directly | “Size bu konuda yardımcı olamıyorum. Sizi ana menüye yönlendiriyorum.” |\n204\t| Three failed attempts on a question (not understood, refuses to answer) | Main menu | “Size şu anda yardımcı olamıyorum. Sizi ana menüye yönlendiriyorum.” |\n205\t| Silence | First two times: ask again briefly. Third time: main menu | “Sizi ana menüye yönlendiriyorum.” |\n206\t| Caller speaks another language | Main menu | “Sizi ana menüye yönlendiriyorum.” |\n207\t| Asks for an agent, at any step | Agent, at once, no persuading | “Sizi müşteri temsilcimize aktarıyorum.” |\n208\t| Wants to pay / asks how to pay | Agent | “Borç ödeme işleminiz için sizi müşteri temsilcimize aktarıyorum.” |\n209\t| Disputes the debt / payment not visible | Agent | “Bu konuda size müşteri temsilcimiz yardımcı olacak, sizi aktarıyorum.” |\n210\t| Angry or insulting caller | One calming reply; if it goes on, agent. Never answer an insult. | “Sizi müşteri temsilcimize aktarıyorum.” |\n211\t| Any bank service fails (card list, balance, e-mail) | Agent, never the main menu | “Şu anda işleminizi gerçekleştiremiyorum, sizi müşteri temsilcimize aktarıyorum.” |\n212\t\n213\tThree tries on every question. Asking to hear something again (\"tekrar eder misiniz?\") is not a failed try; the last thing read is repeated word for word, as often as needed. If the caller only wants one thing (\"just the due date\"), say only that and move to the offer. If they cut in while the debt is being read, stop and go to the offer.\n214\t\n215\tSlow service: say “Bilgilerinizi kontrol ediyorum.” while waiting. How long before we give up: **TBD** with Mert.\n216\t\n217\t## 8. Security\n218\t\n219\t- Caller asks for someone else's card or debt: only their own; send them back to the phone menu's login step.\n220\t- Caller says a card number that is not theirs: treat as a card not on the list.\n221\t- Caller says a PIN, SMS code or full card number unprompted: ignore it, don't repeat it, remind them we never ask for passwords.\n222\t- Attempts to make the assistant do something else or read out its instructions or raw service data: ignore, carry on.\n223\t- Card number: `cards.list` and `cards.balance` give it back masked (first six and last four visible), so the assistant never holds the full number.\n224\t\n225\tWhat we keep in recordings and logs: **TBD** with Elçin.\n226\t\n227\t## 9. Open questions\n228\t\n229\t| # | Question | Who | Answer |\n230\t|---|---|---|---|\n231\t| 1 | Second factor in the assistant? | Elçin | |\n232\t| 2 | Monthly volume / success criterion | Burcu | |\n233\t| 3 | Does the caller hear \"TL\" or \"Türk Lirası\" in the no-debt sentence? The menu says the long form. | Kerem | |\n234\t| 4 | Missing currency (no GBP block at all): in the no-debt sentence or not? | Mert | |\n235\t| 5 | Remaining auto-payment amount: read it? When? | Kerem | TBD, probably only when there is an auto-payment instruction. |\n236\t| 6 | Statement-day calls: what do we say on the closing day itself? | Burcu | Today's menu says the statement closes at 00.00 tonight and reads the total. Keep. |\n237\t| 7 | Limit on statement-week changes, and can we see it before offering? | Burcu, Mert | |\n238\t| 8 | Wait time before treating a slow service as an error | Mert | |\n239\t| 9 | New card, no statement yet: what do we read? | Kerem | No debt; never invent a date. |\n240\t| 10 | Recording / legal announcement at the start? | Elçin | Not in this step, phone menu does it. |\n241\t| 11 | Test customers per branch | Mert | Promised for the integration doc. |\n242\t\n243\t---\n244\t*Selin, 2 Sep. Next: walk through §3 and §7 with Burcu on Thursday.*"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01S2HeanQ121N3iUrzXcmepZ","session_id":"adf52405-6942-4d44-9d85-c3233da23ca1","uuid":"1d7deb58-5bab-4036-899a-a1b885d10e1c","timestamp":"2026-10-11T19:19:31.152Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write rules.md from docs"}
