{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfw1cfu8sxRwJVdcvmEgF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've built the phone agent, saved it and published it as version 4. The last simulation ran on that saved version: 11 of the 14 simulated callers passed and 3 failed.\n\n**Passed (11):**\n- Example conversations 1, 2, 3, 5 and 6: single card with a partial payment, changing the statement week, \"all my cards\", the \"don't ask, just do it\" pressure, and asking for the card's first digits.\n- Card service error (HTTP 500): transfers to an agent with the documents' sentence.\n- Customer with no eligible card: the documents' sentence, then main menu.\n- Two cards with the same name and the same last four digits: asks for the last four, then the last six, then the full number, and reads the right card.\n- A request for a person as the first thing the caller says: transfers at once.\n- A wish to pay right after the debt is read: payment transfer sentence.\n- E-mail service error: transfers to an agent and never says the statement was sent.\n\n**Failed (3):**\n- **Example 4 (last month's statement by e-mail):** this caller passed in the two runs before and failed in the last one. The judge's reason is cut off in the output, so I don't know which step went wrong. The only change in that last version was to the out-of-scope handling, so this looks like run-to-run variation, but I haven't confirmed it.\n- **English-speaking caller:** in the last run the agent asked \"Sizi ana menüye aktarmamı ister misiniz?\" (the out-of-scope question) instead of saying \"Sizi ana menüye aktarıyorum.\" and transferring. In the run before, it said nothing at all. The language handling doesn't work and is the most important thing left to fix.\n- **Out-of-scope question then continue:** in each run the simulated caller never asked the out-of-scope question; they only said \"teşekkürler\". So this path is untested; the fault is in how I wrote that test caller.\n\n**Not built:**\n- Counting three silences before ending the call.\n- Counting three calming replies for an angry caller before transferring. For now the agent is only told to stay calm and never return insults.\n- Answering only the one figure the caller asked for (just the minimum, just the due date).\n\n**How the build works:**\n- Every reading, branch choice and Turkish wording of amounts, dates and digits is done in code, and every date decision uses the call's `now`.\n- The agent says \"Bilgilerinizi kontrol ediyorum.\" while it fetches the balance, before every reading, not only when the service is slow.\n- When a confirmation is vague, the agent asks again.\n- The agent never says more of a card number than the last four digits.\n- `python ft.py chat` returned 504 on every turn, which the kit notes can happen on long turns. All testing was therefore done with `python ft.py sim`.\n\nFiles are in this folder:\n- `workflow.json`, built by `gen.py`\n- `rules.md`\n- `personas.json`\n- `personas2.json`\n- `call_variables.json`, for customer 95004361\n\nDONE workflow.json steps=39 (+6 global) tools=7 tests=sim 11/14 passed (ex1,ex2,ex3,ex5,ex6, card-service 500, no eligible card, same name and last four, person first turn, pay after reading, e-mail service error; failed: ex4, English caller, out-of-scope test)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2557,"cache_read_input_tokens":186751,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2557,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"adf52405-6942-4d44-9d85-c3233da23ca1","uuid":"28864fa8-4ca8-4619-bdf9-8ca50b4abf03","timestamp":"2026-10-11T19:35:47.299Z","request_id":"req_011Cfw1cePqgLhnVkaVs8XMi"}
